IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pta-small-estates`

-- Public Trustee Act 1915, s 6(1)-(3), (6)-(8), with Public Trustee Rules rr 7A and 9 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case. Expected results were written by hand from the deposited text.

§ `REQ-0279 (Haziq scenario) -- an intestate estate of $38,000`

-- A man dies intestate leaving $38,000 in a bank account and no property. The amount prescribed for s 6(1) is $5,000 (r 7A).
-- $38,000 is not less than $5,000, so s 6(1) does not reach the estate, whatever the beneficiaries' means.
#ASSERT `the amount prescribed for section 6(1)` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT NOT `the estate is within the small-estate amount` 38000
#ASSERT NOT `a section 6(1) application may be made` TRUE 38000 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Public Trustee must administer under section 6(1)` TRUE 38000 TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the Public Trustee must refuse the section 6 application` 38000 TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the section 6 route for an estate of` 38000 EQUALS "not s 6(1): only by court order under s 6(6), on proceedings already instituted"
-- The court route has no value limit: on proceedings instituted, if administration by the Public Trustee is expedient and the
-- court has considered its views, the court may order it even at $38,000.
#ASSERT `the court may order the Public Trustee to administer` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE

§ `r 7A, s 6(1) -- the boundary`

#ASSERT `the estate is within the small-estate amount` 4999.99
#ASSERT `the estate is within the small-estate amount` 0
#ASSERT NOT `the estate is within the small-estate amount` 5000
#ASSERT NOT `the estate is within the small-estate amount` 5000.01
#ASSERT NOT `the estate is within the small-estate amount` 50000
#ASSERT `the section 6 route for an estate of` 4000 EQUALS "s 6(1): application to the Public Trustee, who must administer if the beneficiaries are of small means and there is no good reason to refuse"
#ASSERT `the section 6 route for an estate of` 5000 EQUALS "not s 6(1): only by court order under s 6(6), on proceedings already instituted"

§ `s 6(1) -- the duty to administer`

#ASSERT `the Public Trustee must administer under section 6(1)` TRUE 4000 TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Public Trustee must administer under section 6(1)` FALSE 4000 TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Public Trustee must administer under section 6(1)` TRUE 4000 FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Public Trustee must administer under section 6(1)` TRUE 4000 TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Public Trustee must administer under section 6(1)` TRUE 4000 TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `a section 6(1) application may be made` TRUE 4000 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a section 6(1) application may be made` TRUE 4000 FALSE

§ `r 9(1), (3) -- refusal`

#ASSERT NOT `the Public Trustee must refuse the section 6 application` 4000 TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the Public Trustee must refuse the section 6 application` 4000 FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the Public Trustee must refuse the section 6 application` 4000 TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the Public Trustee must refuse the section 6 application` 4000 TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the Public Trustee must refuse the section 6 application` 5000 TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `after a refusal the Public Trustee may still act under other powers` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `after a refusal the Public Trustee may still act under other powers` FALSE

§ `s 6(2), (3), (8) -- vesting and discharge`

#ASSERT `the trust property vests in the Public Trustee` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the trust property vests in the Public Trustee` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the trust property vests in the Public Trustee` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the former trustee is discharged from the liability` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the former trustee is discharged from the liability` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the former trustee is discharged from the liability` FALSE FALSE

§ `s 6(6), (7) -- court order`

#ASSERT `the court may order the Public Trustee to administer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the court may order the Public Trustee to administer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the court may order the Public Trustee to administer` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the court may order the Public Trustee to administer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
